THE FIX SITE (located by the code-graph detective — anchor every criterion to the behaviour THIS code produces):
- src/services/contentstack.ts :: options — This is where the Contentstack SDK Stack is initialized. The `options` object passed to `contentstack.Stack(options)` lacks the `live_preview` configuration — without it the SDK never enters live-preview mode, so no real-time content updates are ever delivered to the app. This is the root cause: the SDK must be configured with live_preview.enable=true (and a management token) before any downstream component can react to CMS edits.
- src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx :: ContentstackProvider — Even with the SDK configured for live preview, the ContentstackProvider provides content as a static value via `useMemo([defaultContent])` — it never re-renders when the SDK pushes updated content. The provider must subscribe to the SDK's `onEntryChange` callback (or `Stack.livePreviewQuery`) and update the context value reactively so all 236+ consumers of `useContent` receive fresh data without a page refresh.
Do NOT write criteria about areas unrelated to this code.


